index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..fcc40b3f55c9624a5549124c315e538b6d79393e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/dev/openabstractions.md
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+# Native OpenAbstractions services
+
+This build adds native IPC model downloads and logging. The existing HTTP,
+engine, UI and packaging paths remain available. Build support with
+`LEMONADE_OPENABSTRACTIONS=ON`. The OA delivery variant also sets
+`LEMONADE_OA_BRANDED_BUILD=ON`, which always enables both features and has no
+off switch. Other OA-linked native builds default off, accept explicit `1`
+opt-ins and `0`, and refuse other switch values. No global environment
+setting is written. An enabled download
+failure is explicit. It never retries through Lemonade HTTP. Default installed
+runtime discovery supplies server identity admission. The historical raw
+`LEMONADE_OA_RUNTIME_ENDPOINT` override is refused.
+
+The OA variant admits its configuration during startup, after `--host`/`--port`
+validation and before any listener or model work. It refuses when
+`LEMONADE_OA_DOWNLOADS` or `LEMONADE_OA_LOGGING` is set to anything but `1`,
+when an OA option or environment setting is invalid, or when the runtime cannot
+serve logging or download jobs. `lemond` and `LemonadeServer` then print
+`OA Lemonade refused: <status>: <detail>` to standard error and exit with 69
+(EX_UNAVAILABLE). `<status>` is `integration_disabled` for a switch set to `0`,
+`invalid_configuration`, the SDK resolution word (usually
+`runtime_unavailable`) or the IPC status name such as `untrusted`. `--help`
+and `--version` never consult the runtime.
+
+Downloads use `abstraction.job/operations@1` and reconciliation@1. The saved
+identity pins URL, content hash, endpoint, logical owner, key and history epoch.
+Malformed or changed saved metadata refuses recovery. Cancellation keeps the
+identity until a terminal observation. Graceful process shutdown stops local
+waiting and result copying while preserving the durable job. Explicit user
+cancellation separately requests job cancellation. Result delivery reuses HttpClient's
+existing hash verification, including Git-blob hashes for non-LFS HF files.
+Logging uses `abstraction.logging/sink@1` through a bounded asynchronous sink.
+Sink shutdown discards its queue and cancels the current IPC wait before joining.
+Saved metadata is validated before cached-file success.
+
+The Windows OA variant defaults its settings and runtime cache to native
+LocalAppData/LemonadeOA/config and cache, outside OA core reset roots. Explicit caller paths
+and cache environment overrides retain their existing meaning. It imports no
+legacy upstream metadata automatically. HF/model cache defaults and overrides
+remain shared durable resources. Its instance mutex has a distinct local-session
+identity. The OA CLI and server require explicit host and port; the CLI refuses automatic
+discovery; explicit scan remains observational. The first serving route uses
+the existing OA provider's controlled private configuration, loopback port and
+owned-child/socket admission. Standalone tray packaging remains pending its
+embedded-server lifecycle readiness proof and actual MSI qualification; no
+guessed default endpoint is selected here.
+Unspecified server broadcast defaults off for the OA variant; explicit server
+host/port/broadcast overrides keep their caller-selected values.
+
+## Exact source inputs
+
+Lemonade upstream stable `v2026.43.3` resolves to
+`b48d190a9b00a417fda9cbf206fcec5691e5578b`. The annotated tag is unsigned.
+The native starting patch is the September stranger IPC patch, SHA256
+`40112fc387ccfbbfe45cdbef5d33039486d1c6570b68ab643590ed367362e763`.
+
+The SDK input is private product snapshot
+`b7457dbd834b3b5cd602e318edb873570a395d4f`. Each consumed `cpp` subtree is
+identical to the following publicly obtainable source commit/tree. These are
+source pins, with no C++ package-tag claim. Preserve each source license.
+
+| Repository | Public commit | cpp tree |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| abstraction-identity | 1267f150df094a372b29080fe110fe82c955c295 | d91a527eaffe1bff6ae9a03c1860abba38ad199f |
+| abstraction-facade | f77d816b427aa25049b10b939cbc04ee9bdaba80 | 731f851bffbef18eb494884df16ed70241e61a78 |
+| abstraction-job | 0e015a123b6111aaabb8b58a4939fe567a95335e | 8a45180be2dccc92851a38c3c0c1536285b8f4ad |
+| abstraction-download | 8acda85d35cec78bf7a4fa1b270150bb152fa8ed | b0316282050500726e01f4935f3331905d99e6ac |
+| abstraction-logging | 962eb6bb6d06cb2e09051aa00d96e5cabb6f7187 | 7b063081ac7cc2f949d72cf66fdb64485f6815ec |
+
+## Build and qualification plan
+
+Use clean sibling SDK source directories and an absolute SDK prefix. Configure
+facade with aggregate OFF, JOBS ON and LOGGING ON; configure download's existing
+request-only target separately. Build and install both using the same static
+MSVC CRT as Lemonade (`CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=MultiThreaded`). The SDK
+CMake owners fetch nothing. Configure Lemonade with the installed prefix and
+`LEMONADE_OPENABSTRACTIONS=ON` plus `LEMONADE_OA_BRANDED_BUILD=ON` for the OA
+variant. Its existing WiX owner prepares a distinct per-user
+`Lemonade (OA build)` product/root/registry/shortcut identity. Fixed component
+codes and the upgrade namespace are deterministic and distinct from upstream;
+the existing fragment generator's ID-prefix option separates harvested web/docs
+components. Normal MSI ProductCode generation and major-upgrade handling remain.
+OA packaging omits PATH mutation, upstream protocol cleanup, process/cleanup
+custom actions, startup and automatic launch.
+It also omits Start menu and desktop shortcuts: OA's resource service starts
+`lemond` and the router reaches it, and the OA variant refuses a launch
+without `--host`/`--port`. The product is removed through the system's
+installed-apps list.
+Its executable payload also carries the existing native `lemond.exe` target for
+the controlled OA provider route. Payload presence does not qualify that route's
+launch, ABI or model behavior.
+
+OA MSI targets require explicit `LEMONADE_OA_MSI_VERSION` (three Windows Installer
+numeric fields within 255.255.65535). `LEMONADE_OA_PACKAGE_MODE=qa` is the default
+and requires filename-safe `LEMONADE_OA_QA_LABEL`, preserving the QA filename and
+normal build dependencies. Explicit `LEMONADE_OA_PACKAGE_MODE=release` requires
+an empty QA label and exact source version `2026.43.3+oa.<OA MSI version>` for
+this pinned upstream. Export that version through the existing
+`tools/source_archive.py --version` before configuring/building the release
+source archive. A QA or git-derived development version refuses release mode.
+
+Release mode's existing `wix_installer_minimal` target packages prepared inputs
+without native/web build dependencies. Build `lemond`, `lemonade`,
+`LemonadeServer` and `web-app` first, then sign the three native executables in
+`BUILD_DIR/Release` through the caller's existing signing owner. Freeze those
+files and all prepared package resources; invoke only the MSI target after
+signing, with no configure/build step in between. The release filename retains
+the upstream and OA versions and omits a QA suffix. Product identity, per-user
+ownership and normal MSI ProductCode semantics are unchanged.
+
+The caller admits the exact signed payload receipt before packaging, then reads
+back every MSI File/Binary stream. Own File PE keys are exactly `lemond.exe`,
+`lemonade.exe` and `LemonadeServer.exe`; the own Binary PE set is empty. Supplier
+WiX UI PE bytes require their separate pinned supplier admission. Extra/changed
+PEs refuse; CMake supplies no signing authority. Sign the resulting MSI through
+the same caller's container owner and verify internal bytes again. The existing
+bundle-app row carries the actual signed MSI digest/size; source and signing
+facts stay beside it. Publication and final receipt schemas belong to that
+existing producer. Current QA0.4 SDK compatibility does not qualify a future0.8
+SDK rebuild merely by selecting release version text.
+ProductVersion is the selected OA version; the output filename also records the
+upstream version and, in QA mode, the QA label. Missing QA version inputs leave native compilation
+available with OA MSI targets disabled. The OA full/Tauri target stays disabled
+pending its lifecycle/protocol closure. The minimal target remains source
+preparation: both installer delivery and the included standalone tray need actual
+qualification before use. Dependency/backend review, full clean builds and
+signed-byte installer qualification remain required. No end-user compiler or
+Python dependency is introduced.
+
+An OA MSI additionally requires `LEMONADE_OA_SDK_LICENSE` to name the license
+from its exact SDK source export. The existing CMake producer copies that file,
+the Lemonade license, and the linked native dependency source notices into its
+licenses payload. OA packaging requires the exact `FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_*`
+source inputs, including dependencies selected through explicit include paths.
+Every admitted notice must exist. The existing WiX harvester
+uses a distinct OA component namespace for this folder; stock installers retain
+their existing payload. The web renderer's generated license files remain in
+the harvested web-app payload. These source controls require actual package
+inspection and signed-byte qualification before distribution.
+
+The OA web build also preserves full license/notice files from its exact
+lock-installed packages under `web-app/licenses`, retaining package-relative
+paths. Linked notices are refused and directory links are not traversed.
+The KaTeX 0.16.45 fonts have separate SIL OFL 1.1 terms in their embedded font
+metadata. `src/web-app/KaTeX-fonts-OFL.txt` carries all twelve reserved family
+names and the full official license, with its exact source URL/hash. The build
+refuses a different KaTeX version until its font notice has been reviewed.
+
+The inert fixture generator `tests/oa_adapter_fixture.py` projects the actual
+saved-identity and shared cache-admission bodies into a small C++ translation
+unit. Its controlled hash answers test admission control flow. Normal upstream
+tests must separately exercise the real hash backend. Full adapter compilation
+against these exact SDK headers passes; linking, installed 0.4 ABI acceptance,
+switch-off parity, cancellation, ambiguous submit recovery, restart continuation,
+native logs and installer behavior remain pending. Runtime tests must use an
+explicitly owned fixture and must never discover the owner's installed runtime.
+# OA QA source identity and Windows wake pipe
+
+The existing `.version` archive override binds this OA QA build to upstream
+`v2026.43.3` (`b48d190a9b00a417fda9cbf206fcec5691e5578b`) as
+`2026.43.3+oa.0.8.0-qa.938`. The separate OA MSI version is `0.8.0` and its
+QA label is `qa.938`.
+
+For the OA Windows build, the existing libwebsockets source transform also
+binds both Windows wake-pipe UDP sockets to loopback. The pinned dependency
+base is `4415e84c095857629863804e941b9e1c2e9347ef`; its original unbound sender
+autobinds to a wildcard endpoint on its first wake signal. The provider's
+socket containment rule remains intact. `tests/oa_lws_fixture.py` emits the
+actual dependency function bodies with the owning transform for a native
+check of both socket-table entries, wake delivery, and cleanup.
